 \label{prop:nonuple}
As an identity of functions in $\mathcal{T}_{\mathbb{C}}\left(q^2x^7\right)$,
\begin{equation} \label{eq:nonuple}
\begin{split}
    (q;q) \left\langle x; q \right\rangle \left\langle qx^2; q^2 \right\rangle^2 \left\langle x^2; q^2 \right\rangle
    &=
    - \frac{\vect{q^2x^7}{1} + \vect{q^2x^7}{2}}{\left\langle q^2 ; q^7 \right\rangle^2 \left\langle q; q^7\right\rangle}
    +
    \frac{\vect{q^2x^7}{0} + \vect{q^2x^7}{3}}{\left\langle q ; q^7 \right\rangle^2 \left\langle q^3; q^7\right\rangle}
    \\[4pt]
    &
    + 
    q\frac{\vect{q^2x^7}{-1} + \vect{q^2x^7}{4}}{\left\langle q^3 ; q^7 \right\rangle^2 \left\langle q^2; q^7\right\rangle} 
    - 
    q\frac{2\vect{q^2x^7}{5}}{\left\langle q; q^7\right\rangle \left\langle q^2; q^7 \right\rangle \left\langle q^3; q^7 \right\rangle }.
\end{split}
\end{equation}

