From \cref{thm:twisted-rog-ram-var} and \cref{cor:kind2}, one obtains
\[
    \begin{pmatrix}
    \vect{qx^2-x}{0} \vspace{0.1cm}\\
    \vect{qx^2-x}{1}
    \end{pmatrix}
    =
    \begin{pmatrix}
    A(q) & B(q) \\
    C(q) & D(q)
    \end{pmatrix}
    \begin{pmatrix}
    \left(x^{-1}; q\right)^{-1} \vect{qx^2}{0}
    \vspace{0.1cm}\\
    \left(x^{-1}; q\right)^{-1} \vect{qx^2}{1}
    \end{pmatrix}.
\]
Writing $\left(x^{-1}; q\right)^{-1} = \sum_{m \ge 0} (q; q)^{-m} x^{-m}$ and restricting to powers $x^n$ with $n \ge 0$ yields
\[
    \begin{pmatrix}
    \vect{qx^2-x}{0}_{\ge 1} \vspace{0.1cm}\\
    \vect{qx^2-x}{1}_{\ge 1}
    \end{pmatrix}
    =
    \begin{pmatrix}
    A(q) & B(q) \\
    C(q) & D(q)
    \end{pmatrix}
    \begin{pmatrix}
    \sum_{2n > m \ge 0} \frac{q^{n^2}}{(q; q)_m} x^{2n-m} 
    \vspace{0.1cm} \\ 
    \sum_{2n\ge m \ge 0} \frac{q^{n^2+n}}{(q; q)_m} x^{2n+1-m} 
    \end{pmatrix}.
\]
Taking $x = -1$ recovers the first claimed equality in light of \cref{eq:truncations}. The second claimed equality follows analogously by taking $q \mapsto q^2$ above, and then $x = -q^{-1}$.

\[
    \begin{pmatrix}
    \vect{qx^2-x}{0} \vspace{0.1cm}\\
